+- **The result of a pointer press.** A click of **Space cards** or **Dismiss suggestion** whose `detail` is 1 or more (a mouse click, a tap or a pen press; Enter, Space and a scripted `click()` report 0) and that the viewport gate lets act first measures the panel's box (`getBoundingClientRect` width and height) and hands it to the canvas with the action. In the same React commit that removes the panel, the canvas then shows a **result** in its place: `SpaceCardsResult` in `editor/SpaceCardsOffer.tsx`, in the panel's own wrapper (so before the flow, `nokey`, the same absolute place and `z-[5]`), with the panel's own classes (background, border, shadow, rounding and padding) and exactly that width and height, saying **Spaced _n_ cards.**, **Cards were not spaced: they are no longer all in one spot.** or **Suggestion dismissed.** The visible line leaves out "Undo puts them back." because the result can outlive later edits; the announcement still says it. **Why.** A native check at 512 px found the panel's left part covering **Zoom Out** at (93, 290): the first press of a double click hit **Space cards**, the panel left, and the second press of the same run hit **Zoom Out**, which zoomed the view out (1.30597 to 1.08831) before the one fit took it to 0.5. A press cannot be sorted into "belongs to the same run" when it starts: its click count arrives with `mousedown` and `click`, after the pointer handlers, the Shift selection path, a route handle's own `pointerdown` and a touch press have already acted. So the panel's place stays occupied instead. The result has no button, no `tabindex`, no handler, no live region of its own (the canvas's polite region already announced it, once) and unselectable text (`select-none`); a press on it does nothing, and nothing about it is prevented, stopped, delayed, replayed or synthesized, so it reaches no pane, d3-zoom or d3-drag, route handle, port or zoom control. Focus stays on the canvas root; the one step, the one save and the on